  "notes": "PROTOCOL SPLIT: PHYTMO records six upper-limb exercises on the arm and forearm units and fourteen lower-limb ones on the shin and thigh units; the converter records which group each session belongs to in its session id, and `streams` above is derived from that, not from what survived windowing. Scoring an arm stream against the dataset-wide 20 would charge it for 14 labels its acquisition configuration never records.\nOPEN DESIGN QUESTION, not yet resolved: ten of the twenty labels are exact `X` / `X_performed_incorrectly` pairs. Under a language-conditioned candidate scorer those pairs are near-indistinguishable BY CONSTRUCTION, independent of encoder quality, so a flat 20-way (or 14-way / 6-way) number understates the model on exercise identity and overstates the difficulty of nothing in particular. The intended reporting is exercise identity as one cell and correct-versus-incorrect execution as a separate binary cell; that needs a harness change and is deliberately NOT faked here by dropping the incorrect variants. See docs/data/DATASET_EXPANSION_AUDIT_2026-08-11.md section 2.4."
